<title>GERMANY: Key German sugar area reports good beet weather.</title>
<headline>Key German sugar area reports good beet weather.</headline>
<dateline>BRAUNSCHWEIG, Germany 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Key northern German sugar producer Zuckerverbund Nord AG (ZVN) said sugar beet weights in the ZVN growing regions were above those last year as a result of favourable rainfall.</p>
<p>A company official said the beet was looking healthy and leaf weights and structures were developing along the lines seen last year.</p>
<p>But with two months to go until harvesting, he cautioned that current conditions could change very quickly.</p>
<p>Yields of 50 tonnes per hectare (tph), predicted by ZVN earlier this month, were possible but it was too early to comment on the likelihood.</p>
<p>Germany's average beet yield in 1996 was 50.7 tph while in Lower Saxony, where ZVN operates, the yield was 48.4 tph.</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
